<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45722" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suāsus</span></b> , ūs,
			m.
		suadeo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an advising</i>, <i>persuading</i>
			(ante- and post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ob meum suasum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Phorm. 5, 1, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per vim, vel per suasum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					9, 2, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jussu et increpitu ea expellens, non suasu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 8</span></i>
			 (but not <i><span class="en">Plaut. Pers. 4, 4, 48</span></i>; v. Ritschl
			ad loc.).</div>
